Apple last month announced a new Mac mini and a new Mac Studio. Both machines start shipping on Tuesday, September 22, which means they will launch in the same month as new iPhones, Apple Watches, and AirPods. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/11/Apple-Store-Logo-Livat-Beijing.jpeg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1027231" /><br/>
Apple is expected to introduce the unannounced products at its annual iPhone fall event, which is this year carrying the tagline "<a href="http://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/26/apple-iphone-event-2026/">Surprise and shine.</a>" The event takes place on Wednesday, September 9, making this month one of the busiest Apple has had in a while.<br/>
<br/>
We should therefore see eight new Apple products go on sale before the end of September:<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong>Mac mini (M6 and M5 Pro)</strong>: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-announces-2026-mac-mini/">Announced</a> last week, the new models start shipping September 22, with prices starting at &#36;899.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Mac Studio (M5 Max and M5 Ultra)</strong>: Also <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-announces-new-mac-studio-with-m5-ultra-chip/">announced</a> last week, the new models begin shipping September 22, with prices starting at &#36;2,499.</li><br/>
<li><strong>iPhone 18 Pro</strong>: The flagship device set to be unveiled at Apple's fall event, with a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/01/23/iphone-18-pro-alleged-dynamic-island-size/">smaller Dynamic Island</a> and a A20 Pro chip.</li><br/>
<li><strong>iPhone 18 Pro Max</strong>: The device is rumored to gain a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/18/iphone-18-pro-max-camera-upgrade-exclusive/">camera upgrade</a> exclusive to the larger model, alongside a bigger battery.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Foldable iPhone</strong>: The company's first foldable is expected to have a ~5.5-inch display when closed, and a ~7.8-inch display when open, plus a super thin design with minimal crease and a durable hinge. It could be called "iPhone Ultra."</li><br/>
<li><strong>Apple Watch Series 12</strong>: Apple's upcoming smartwatch is expected feature fitness tracking improvements and a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/26/apple-watch-series-12-ultra-4-features-rumors/">faster S12 chip</a>.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Apple Watch Ultra 4</strong>: Apple's flagship rugged watch is expected to be updated alongside the Series 12, gaining the same S12 chip.</li><br/>
<li><strong>AirPods 5</strong>: The new earbuds were <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/18/unreleased-airpods-5-models-referenced-macos-26-7/">referenced in macOS 26.7</a> and are reportedly ready for release, suggesting a launch alongside the new iPhones.</li><br/>
</ul>Apple isn't going to release a standard iPhone 18 in September 2026. The lineup will instead focus on more expensive iPhones. The ‌iPhone 18‌, iPhone 18e, and iPhone Air 2 will come out in spring 2027 instead. Apple does not plan to refresh the Apple Watch SE this year.<br/>
<br/>
Apple has held its fall event in the first two weeks of September in each of the last several years, with new iPhones going on sale the following Friday.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's "iPhone Ultra" was recently believed to have a delayed launch running into October, even though it's expected to be announced at the same time as the iPhone 18 Pro models. However, <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/01/foldable-iphone-ultra-magsafe/">said this week</a> he would be "very surprised" if the foldable did not come out at the same time as the Pro iPhones or "very close to it."<br/>
<br/>
"Either on the same launch date, a dual launch, or coming out within weeks later. This idea of a late October, November launch, massive delays, supply chain issues, I don't believe to be the case," he said. <br/>
